
Pattern 3 — Abstract Factory

================================================================================================================================================
1. The problem it solves
    Imagine an insurance platform that supports two insurance product families:
          - Retail insurance: motor policy documents, retail invoices, retail notifications.
          - Corporate insurance: corporate policy documents, corporate invoices, corporate notifications.

    You want to ensure that when the application selects the corporate product family, 
it creates compatible corporate components rather than accidentally 
mixing retail and corporate components.

Abstract Factory provides an interface for creating families of related objects without specifying their concrete classes.
================================================================================================================================================
🏭 FACTORY METHOD vs ABSTRACT FACTORY

+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| FEATURE              | FACTORY METHOD           | ABSTRACT FACTORY         |
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| 🎯 Focus              | Creates a Product        | Creates a family of      |
|                      | through a factory method | related Products         |
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| 🏗️ Structure          | Commonly uses Creator    | Commonly uses a Factory  |
|                      | inheritance              | interface                |
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| ⚙️ Creation           | Typically one factory    | Multiple factory methods |
|                      | method per Creator       | for related Products     |
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| 🔄 Extension          | Add a Concrete Creator   | Add a Concrete Factory   |
|                      | for a new creation       | for a new product family |
|                      | strategy                 |                          |
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| 📄 Example            | Select a Motor Policy    | Create compatible policy |
|                      | Document Generator       | document, validator, and |
|                      |                          | notification components  |
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+
| 🧠 Key question       | Which Product should     | Which family of related  |
|                      | this Creator create?     | Products should I create?|
+----------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+

REMEMBER:
Factory Method  → Create a Product through an overridable method.
Abstract Factory → Create a family of related Products.

================================================================================================================================================

🏭 3. ABSTRACT FACTORY — DESIGN STRUCTURE

                 InsuranceComponentFactory
                    (Abstract Factory)
                            |
                 createDocumentGenerator() 
                createNotificationSender()
                            |
             +--------------+--------------+
             |                             |
             ▼                             ▼
       RetailFactory                CorporateFactory
      (Concrete Factory)           (Concrete Factory)
             |                             |
       +-----+------+                +-----+------+
       |            |                |            |
       ▼            ▼                ▼            ▼
 Retail Document  Retail          Corporate   Corporate
   Generator     Notification      Document   Notification
                  Sender          Generator      Sender

🧠 KEY CONCEPT:
Each Concrete Factory creates a compatible family
of related products.

RetailFactory    → Retail document + Retail notification
CorporateFactory → Corporate document + Corporate notification


The client depends on the factory interface, not the concrete factory classes.
================================================================================================================================================

I would choose Abstract Factory when the application needs to create multiple related 
products that belong to the same family and must remain compatible.

With independent Factory Methods, each product's creation can be handled separately,
which may allow incompatible combinations. Abstract Factory groups these creation 
operations behind a single factory abstraction, so the client selects a family 
and obtains its related products through that factory.

The trade-off is additional interfaces and concrete factory classes. 
It is most valuable when product families are a meaningful architectural concept; 
if the application creates only one independent product, Abstract Factory may introduce unnecessary complexity.


